cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it as below. Once an archived release
  has a DOI (e.g. through the Zenodo–GitHub integration), cite that DOI.
type: software
title: "ASTRA — Agent-orchestrated Simulation Testbed for Research on Awareness (MCP server, FCS layer)"
version: 3.1.0
date-released: 2026-09-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/christophejlegros-lgtm/ASTRA-Unified-ResearchLab-MCP-FCS-v3.1.0"
authors:
  - family-names: Legros
    given-names: Christophe Jean
    affiliation: "Assistance Multi IA, Geneva"
    email: Assistant-Multi-IA@proton.me
abstract: >-
  Model Context Protocol server exposing 70 simulation and analysis tools to AI
  assistants: a LIF+STDP spiking network, a JEPA-style world model, computed
  proxies named after theories of consciousness, simulated bridges to
  biocomputing platforms, and an executable layer for the research programme of
  substrate-constrained functionalism (FCS). All biological and physiological
  data are simulated; the consciousness-related indices are proxies, not
  measurements. Third-party components keep their own licences (see
  THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
keywords:
  - model context protocol
  - spiking neural network
  - active inference
  - consciousness science
  - biocomputing
  - epistemology
